<title>GERMANY: Salomon says cuts Vereinsbank to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>Salomon says cuts Vereinsbank to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment bank Salomon Brothers said on Monday it had cut its recommendation on Bayerische Vereinsbank AG to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; after news of its plans to merge with Bayerische Hypotheken und Wechsel-Bank AG.</p>
<p>Analyst Matthew Czepliewicz, speaking from London, told Reuters he welcomed the merger news as a move to consolidate in the banking industry but was sceptical about the scale of hoped-for synergies arising from the merger.</p>
<p>&quot;Vereinsbank shares have risen 90 percent in the past year. I think it has seen a very nice move so far and I don't see much more in there,&quot; Czepliewicz said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
